The record is Arizona HB2492 (2022), coded as one record group across three pages:

- **Vote page** — `DUNN Y` at House Third Reading, `Passed 31-26-3-0-0`. One Dunn in the roster, chamber named on the page, 26 No of 60 so not near-unanimous.
- **Bill text (Chapter 99)** — `provision_quote` from the amended §16-121.01(C), which requires registration applications to be accompanied by satisfactory evidence of citizenship and directs rejection otherwise. That subsection carries no `[deleted: …]` fence, unlike §16-101, so it is safe to quote as the provision.
